{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>When the Most High gave nations their inheritance.</b> When the Holy One, blessed be He, gave the nations their allotted inheritance, He flooded them and swept them away." "<b>When He separated the children of man.</b> When He scattered the generation of the Dispersion, it was in His hand to obliterate them from the world — but He did not do so; rather, <b>He established the boundaries of peoples</b> — He sustained them and did not destroy them." "<b>According to the number of the children of Israel.</b> For the number of the children of Israel who were destined to come from the descendants of Shem, and for the number of the seventy souls of the children of Israel who went down to Egypt, He established <b>the boundaries of peoples</b> — seventy languages."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:11.044418531Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}